{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1462867-refined-apostles-an-attempt-to-create-a-super-template","id":1462867,"title":"Refined Apostles: An attempt to create a Super-Template","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-05T20:55:13-07:00","id":1462867,"title":"Refined Apostles: An attempt to create a Super-Template","content":"This is essentially my first draft for a way to give Promethean characters a &quot;Super Template&quot; while still having the New Dawn actually be meaningful. Based partly on some suggestions by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12981_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12981\" data-vbnamecard=\"12981\">RomulusGloriosus</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1050092-house-rules-a-brighter-new-dawn\">here</a>, I added my own flavoring to the mix to A) Not plagiarize, and B) Justify the &quot;Super&quot; part of the template. So, here's what I have so far, feel free to ask questions or give suggestions!<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Refined Apostles</u></b><br /> <br /> Originating from the Greek &quot;<i>Apostolos</i>&quot;, or &quot;Messenger,&quot; the Refined Apostles are simultaneously a goal post for many Created as well as a word of warning. They are those Prometheans who, before the New Dawn, dedicated themselves fully to one refinement in particular, yet still branched out enough to have completed the New Dawn to one degree or another. As a result of their devotion, they have retained a measure of their alchemical power as humans, a boon to be sure for some Prometheans who, while eager to become &quot;real,&quot; still enjoy some of the benefits that their abilities bring. Attempting to become one however requires an absurd investment of Vitriol, time and sanity, and more often then not leads one to becoming a Petrificatus or simply dead. And yet, there are still a lucky few out there, less than 1 per year, who manage to succeed, becoming avatars and &quot;Messengers&quot; of their Refinements just as much as Qashmallim do for the Principle.<br /> <br /> How to walk on the path of Apostleship:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><u>Every Alembic available to a particular Refinement (8 in total) MUST be calcified using Vitriol XP.</u> Most Prometheans, upon hearing of this step, immediately forsake the road, recognizing (not unfairly) that it is too heavy of a burden for an individual who is already searching for scraps of Vitriol to use in their journey. Some rumors say that even the current Apostles once used the Lacuna to obtain the needed Vitriol before reaching the New Dawn, but these are unconfirmed.</li> <li><u>The aspiring Created must forge themselves a specific Athanor, an &quot;Apostolic Mantle,&quot; for their chosen Refinement.</u> Doing this does NOT refund the Vitriol XP spent on calcifying. Sacrifices must be made in order to clear the road ahead of distractions.<ul><li>&quot;Apostolic Mantle&quot;</li> <li>Reduce the Pyros cost of Alembics within the Transmutation by 1. While Dampening the Fire, Alembics within the Transmutation ALWAYS treat Azoth as if it was the original value, not the diminished one. Finally, the Promethean is treated as always possessing the Refinement Condition and method for earning Beats (treated as either normal beats or Vitriol beats).</li> </ul></li> <li><u>Upon achieving the New Dawn, the Promethean must choose to retain their memories of the Pilgrimage.</u> Would-be Apostles who choose instead to embrace their new lives only receive the benefits of the &quot;Role Call&quot; trait (see below) and a guarantee of protection by the Principle that their new existence will not be interfered with by outside supernatural parties.</li> </ol>Apostle Systems:<br /> <br /> Apostles are humans who begin their existence with a &quot;Greater Template&quot; according to Imperial Practices. They use the &quot;Magnitude&quot; power stat, and start at Magnitude (Total Completed Refinements / 2, rounded DOWN). A Promethean who completed the bare minimum of Refinements would start play with a Magnitude of 2, while one who went the full distance with 10 Refinements would begin with a Magnitude of 5. In addition, those Apostles who somehow completed all 10 refinements can choose any Alembic they learned throughout play to retain, besides their fixed Alembics.<br /> <br /> Apostles possess a number of traits, seen below:<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated to the Principle:</b> Apostles retain all of the Alembics available for their chosen Refinement, as well as the benefits of the Apostolic Mantle Athanor. Apostles add their Magnitude in Doors whenever a character attempts to dissuade them from their Refinement or a principle related to it. In addition, Apostles can always teach their Refinements to Prometheans willing to learn, and if an Apostle were to create a new Promethean, they would automatically begin in the Apostle's Refinement (breaking the normal rules of character creation.)<br /> <br /> <b>Self-Contained:</b> Apostles naturally produce and retain as Prometheans do, but their perfected bodies do not leak the substance out. Apostles do not suffer or cause Disquiet nor do they suffer from Torment. An Apostle CAN however produce or grow a Wasteland through spending large amounts of Pyros (11 - Magnitude). In addition, Apostles do not suffer from Conditions due to their Pyros as Alchemists do.<br /> <br /> <b>Refined Avatar:</b> When using Refinement Alembics, the Apostle treats their Magnitude as being twice as high (both for dice pools and persistent effects.) By spending a point of Willpower and the necessary amount of Pyros, the Apostle can use their Refinement as being an Influence with a dot level equal to their Magnitude. This can take a few different forms:<ul><li>An Influence based upon the symbolic metal of the Refinement (Gold, Silver, etc.)</li> <li>An Influence based on the Refinement's area of focus (Mortality, Mystery, etc.)</li> <li>An Influence based on one of the Refinement's Transmutations (Deception, Mesmerism, Sensorium, Spiritus, etc.)</li> <li>Any Influence allowed by the Storyteller which ties back into the Refinement and it's ideals.</li> </ul><b>Role Call:</b> As expressions of Refinements, Apostles can take on the &quot;roles&quot; which embody the Refinement. When acting within one of these Roles, an Apostle automatically improves their impression level by one stage. They also gain a dot of Anonymity (which can stack with other sources) as long as they act &quot;in-character.&quot; This dot explicitly does NOT conflict with any dots in Fame the character possesses. An Apostle celebrity for example might be known far and wide for their Hollywood premier, but their personal life won't be looked into (or at least, not easily.)<br /> <br /> <b>Sanctified Soul:</b> By tying themselves so deeply to a Refinement, an Apostle secures their soul from tampering and usurpation. Whenever an effect would target the Apostle's soul, they can spend a point of Pyros to begin a Clash of Wills, using their (Highest Resistance Attribute) + Magnitude x 2. If the roll fails, the Apostle can reroll their dice by spending another point of Pyros. The Apostle can do this as many times as necessary, sidestepping the normal Per-Turn limit of Pyros.<br /> <br /> Character Advancement:<br /> <br /> Despite advancing as far as they have, Apostles can still progress in their abilities, further dedicating themselves to the concepts they hold dear. The following costs use normal XP:<br /> <br /> Trait (Cost)<br /> Attributes (4)<br /> Skills (2)<br /> Skill Specialty (1)<br /> Merit (1)<br /> &quot;Outside&quot; Alembic (4)<sup>1</sup><br /> Magnitude (Max: 5) (10)<br /> <br /> <sub>1</sub>: &quot;Outside&quot; in this case refers to Alembics outside of the Apostle's Refinement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T23:03:12-07:00","id":1462875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1462867-refined-apostles-an-attempt-to-create-a-super-template#post1462867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attempting to become one however requires an absurd investment of Vitriol, time and sanity, and more often then not leads one to becoming a Petrificatus or simply dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>The conditions for becoming a Petrificatus are such that a Promethean who's basically completed their Pilgrimage isn't going to become one \u2014 the state is not unlike becoming a zi'ir in Werewolf 2e, where you have to really badly mess up to get there and being a typical player character specimen of your monster-type makes it harder still.<br /> <br /> As far as &quot;dead&quot; goes\u2026 well, it hasn't stopped the Osirans before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T08:11:38-07:00","id":1462893,"title":"","content":"This is pretty nifty stuff (and homebrew Promethean content is thin on the ground so more is always welcome). I dig their potential uses as a story hook for various ends (Refinement tutor being the most obvious, but other potentialities dangle and glitter so tantalizingly). It's also a great option I think for players who want to continue playing their character after attaining the New Dawn while still being able to hold their own against Created-level threats (or helping to bridge the gap between their former throngmates and the limpid-yet-hazy human world).<br /> <br /> Although you mention that Apostles &quot;naturally produce and retain [Pyros I assume] as Prometheans do,&quot; it might be a good idea to spell out what exactly that entails. Do they regain Pyros at sunrise? Can they still replenish from ensconcing themselves in their former Lineage's element?<br /> <br /> I'm a little cautious about giving Influences to PC options, due to their openness and ambiguity. The only instances I can think of in official material that allow players to gain Influences are in Werewolf (where you're limited to the four classical elements locked behind four different Renown-types) and Geist (where either you're limited to a single Influence at the risk of leaving your body vulnerable, or you're playing one of the Absent whose section maintains a tacit understanding that your Influences conform to those things important to a Rank 2 ghost). What is it theme-wise that Refined Avatar is meant to accomplish (besides making Apostles feel more ethereal)?<br /> <br /> Great job all around on this. You know, thinking about it, there has to be at least <i>one</i> Promethean who's tried making a new Created out of an Apostle's corpse: Wonder what the consequences of that would be. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T13:27:51-07:00","id":1462925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1462867-refined-apostles-an-attempt-to-create-a-super-template?p=1462893#post1462893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty nifty stuff (and homebrew Promethean content is thin on the ground so more is always welcome). I dig their potential uses as a story hook for various ends (Refinement tutor being the most obvious, but other potentialities dangle and glitter so tantalizingly). It's also a great option I think for players who want to continue playing their character after attaining the New Dawn while still being able to hold their own against Created-level threats (or helping to bridge the gap between their former throngmates and the limpid-yet-hazy human world).<br /> <br /> Although you mention that Apostles &amp;quot;naturally produce and retain [Pyros I assume] as Prometheans do,&amp;quot; it might be a good idea to spell out what exactly that entails. Do they regain Pyros at sunrise? Can they still replenish from ensconcing themselves in their former Lineage's element?<br /> <br /> I'm a little cautious about giving Influences to PC options, due to their openness and ambiguity. The only instances I can think of in official material that allow players to gain Influences are in Werewolf (where you're limited to the four classical elements locked behind four different Renown-types) and Geist (where either you're limited to a single Influence at the risk of leaving your body vulnerable, or you're playing one of the Absent whose section maintains a tacit understanding that your Influences conform to those things important to a Rank 2 ghost). What is it theme-wise that Refined Avatar is meant to accomplish (besides making Apostles feel more ethereal)?<br /> <br /> Great job all around on this. You know, thinking about it, there has to be at least <i>one</i> Promethean who's tried making a new Created out of an Apostle's corpse: Wonder what the consequences of that would be. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>First, thanks for the review! I'm glad to see that you enjoy it, as I was a bit worried that the overall reception would be a bit more negative. Now, for your points: <br /> <br /> They do regain Pyros with the sunrise, but NOT from their former element, that's something I'll have to edit when I'm not on lunch break.<br /> <br /> The implementation of Influences was... something of a tug-of-war I had internally. I wanted something that would demonstrate the character's &quot;allegiance&quot; of sorts to the Refinement and be suitably powerful enough as a &quot;super template&quot; of sorts. My OTHER option was to have a character-unique &quot;4 dot&quot; power which united all of the themes of a Transmutation or even the Refinement, a la Ciphers from Demon the Descent or 7-dot powers from TC: Aeon. The issue with that was that I had no idea what rules or guidelines I could use for that. I could likely create something later, but I figured that Influences as an established ruleset would just be easier to implement.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'd rule it as the new Promethean beginning in the Apostle's Refinement, but nothing else. Otherwise you really get into the weeds with how that's supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T19:02:18-07:00","id":1463041,"title":"","content":"This is pretty good! Reminds me somewhat of 1E's Athanors but way better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T18:26:22-07:00","id":1463272,"title":"","content":"I've given some further thought as to the idea of 4-dot powers uniting the Refinement together. While I'm still not sure as to XP costs for that, or any other requirements, here's an example I thought up for Stannum:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Arcing Purge</b></u><br /> By employing the use of Electrification to carry a current of flux repulsing energy, the Apostle can shoot out a bouncing strand of lightning that burns out the Disquiet in people's bodies... violently.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4 Pyros<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Dexterity + Athletics + Magnitude<br /> Treat the bolt of lightning as a (Disquiet)B weapon which can tossed at any opponent within direct line of sight. Once the bolt has hit an enemy, it immediately attacks another nearby enemy suffering from the Disquieted Condition using the same dice roll, -1 success. This continues until there are no more Disquieted enemies, or no more successes. Any enemies hit by the attack immediately lose the Disquieted Condition without resolving. By spending a point of Willpower, the damage can be made to be Aggravated instead. Dramatic Failures (as shown below) can only occur on the FIRST roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The purging lightning flickers through the Apostle's form, dealing (Magnitude)L damage and removing (Magnitude) points of pyros.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The lightning does not arc to the target.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The attack works as specified, continuing on until there are no more targets or successes.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As above, and the victim does not suffer a penalty to their next roll to resist Disquiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","user":"Critian Caceorte","date":". 10-09-2021, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T07:43:31-07:00","id":1463311,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s a pretty good ability I feel. The dramatic failure effect feels fair to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T02:34:22-07:00","id":1464340,"title":"","content":"Does the &quot;apostolic mantle&quot; erase or prevent the possibility of refunding Vitriol through a Refinement Furnace?<br /> <br /> I can't be the only one who conceived of the strategy of using the Vitriol refund mechanic to calcify every single Alembic. In the Refinement of Lead my character would plot how to turn his organs or convenient jewelry into Athanors. Maybe it is sleep deprivation but do you have a rule against multiple &quot;apostolic mantles&quot; from being created?<br /> <br /> I once toyed with a similar idea, never got as far as you did, but it involved having it &quot;both ways&quot;. Just like how the Dragons of the Ordo Dracul want the best of humanity and vampirism without the problems of either. The Promethean would gain a soul that was also a crucible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T08:15:13-07:00","id":1464384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1462867-refined-apostles-an-attempt-to-create-a-super-template?p=1464340#post1464340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the &quot;apostolic mantle&quot; erase or prevent the possibility of refunding Vitriol through a Refinement Furnace?<br /> <br /> I can't be the only one who conceived of the strategy of using the Vitriol refund mechanic to calcify every single Alembic. In the Refinement of Lead my character would plot how to turn his organs or convenient jewelry into Athanors. Maybe it is sleep deprivation but do you have a rule against multiple &quot;apostolic mantles&quot; from being created?<br /> <br /> I once toyed with a similar idea, never got as far as you did, but it involved having it &quot;both ways&quot;. Just like how the Dragons of the Ordo Dracul want the best of humanity and vampirism without the problems of either. The Promethean would gain a soul that was also a crucible.</div> </div> </div> </div>For that specific Refinement, yes. In fact, might as well make it official, if you get an Exceptional Success on the Mantle creation roll, you get a Refinement Mentor, NOT a Furnace. For any other refinement that you somehow finish all three roles for... no, you'd still get your Vitriol back. I just think it's difficult to <i>have</i> other fixed alembics when you're focusing so much on just one. Keeping in mind what I've seen from other player's experience suggesting that a Role takes around ~6 sessions to fulfill, and that you'll want to spend Vitriol on improving Pilgrimage ON TOP OF the process to becoming an Apostle, I just don't think it's likely that you'll even have anything leftover for other Alembics.<br /> <br /> As for the second point, Apostolic Mantles are one per Promethean, and you can only create one for yourself. So yes, only 1 Refinement. <i>However,</i> that doesn't mean that you couldn't <i>use</i> Refinement Furnaces you've created for other Refinements as an Apostle. So, what you could do is first complete all of the roles in your chosen refinement, invest a ton of Vitriol into the necessary alembic fixing, and then the mantle, and then after that any other roles you complete can be used to fund those Vitriol costs and open up for Athanor creation once you complete all three of another Refinement. The one downside is that doing this method, getting the Mantle and then one or more Refinement furnaces, means that you are either spending an INCREDIBLE amount of time completing all of this, time the campaign might not even have, or you are preparing for a 4-5 Refinement human which isn't the best result to get.<br /> <br /> Besides all of that, thanks for checking this little project out! I'm currently working on creating &quot;example&quot; Apostles for each of the refinement. In terms of overall population, I think it's fair to say, considering how many Prometheans fail to complete the New Dawn in the first place, that the current Apostle population is less than 10, and never more than the upper teens. Also, there have been so few Stannum Apostles throughout history because Torment is one of those things that most newly made humans want to even <i>think</i> about the least. In contrast, either Aurum or Mercurius have had the most Apostles (Aurum because of how many Prometheans want to better understand and get closer to humanity, Mercurius because of how much the idea of crafting a Mantle appeals to their craftsman sensibilities.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T20:38:13-07:00","id":1466879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1462867-refined-apostles-an-attempt-to-create-a-super-template?p=1464384#post1464384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that specific Refinement, yes. In fact, might as well make it official, if you get an Exceptional Success on the Mantle creation roll, you get a Refinement Mentor, NOT a Furnace. For any other refinement that you somehow finish all three roles for... no, you'd still get your Vitriol back. I just think it's difficult to <i>have</i> other fixed alembics when you're focusing so much on just one. Keeping in mind what I've seen from other player's experience suggesting that a Role takes around ~6 sessions to fulfill, and that you'll want to spend Vitriol on improving Pilgrimage ON TOP OF the process to becoming an Apostle, I just don't think it's likely that you'll even have anything leftover for other Alembics.<br /> <br /> As for the second point, Apostolic Mantles are one per Promethean, and you can only create one for yourself. So yes, only 1 Refinement. <i>However,</i> that doesn't mean that you couldn't <i>use</i> Refinement Furnaces you've created for other Refinements as an Apostle. So, what you could do is first complete all of the roles in your chosen refinement, invest a ton of Vitriol into the necessary alembic fixing, and then the mantle, and then after that any other roles you complete can be used to fund those Vitriol costs and open up for Athanor creation once you complete all three of another Refinement. The one downside is that doing this method, getting the Mantle and then one or more Refinement furnaces, means that you are either spending an INCREDIBLE amount of time completing all of this, time the campaign might not even have, or you are preparing for a 4-5 Refinement human which isn't the best result to get.<br /> <br /> Besides all of that, thanks for checking this little project out! I'm currently working on creating &amp;quot;example&amp;quot; Apostles for each of the refinement. In terms of overall population, I think it's fair to say, considering how many Prometheans fail to complete the New Dawn in the first place, that the current Apostle population is less than 10, and never more than the upper teens. Also, there have been so few Stannum Apostles throughout history because Torment is one of those things that most newly made humans want to even <i>think</i> about the least. In contrast, either Aurum or Mercurius have had the most Apostles (Aurum because of how many Prometheans want to better understand and get closer to humanity, Mercurius because of how much the idea of crafting a Mantle appeals to their craftsman sensibilities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what happens if I already refunded the Vitriol before I made the Mantle?<br /> <br /> Another thought. The final results of the New Dawn depend on how many Refinements were completed, and an exceptional success acts as one more Refinement. I have heard this describe as rigid, but my interpretation is that the reason the system only accounts for ten is because there are only ten Refinements and that inventing more is will allow more. If ten more Refinements were produced and my assumption correct, either of our ideas may come true just as a result of overachievement. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T20:39:41-07:00","id":1466880,"title":"","content":"Also, would combining your idea with the Refinement of Flux be too much of a paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T17:48:54-08:00","id":1467396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1462867-refined-apostles-an-attempt-to-create-a-super-template?p=1466879#post1466879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, what happens if I already refunded the Vitriol before I made the Mantle?<br /> <br /> Another thought. The final results of the New Dawn depend on how many Refinements were completed, and an exceptional success acts as one more Refinement. I have heard this describe as rigid, but my interpretation is that the reason the system only accounts for ten is because there are only ten Refinements and that inventing more is will allow more. If ten more Refinements were produced and my assumption correct, either of our ideas may come true just as a result of overachievement. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for not answering your question right away, I haven't checked in here the past few days.<br /> <br /> So, the Mantle is an Athanor, and you can only make 1 Athanor per Refinement. Thus, if you created the Mantle, there's no chance of you creating a Refinement Furnace (I even made sure to state that you do NOT get a free Refinement Furnace from an exceptional success.) I don't know of any other way to refund the Vitriol besides that.<br /> <br /> Technically speaking, in the history of PtC there have been 12 refinements (the five simple, the five complex, Flux and then Pneuma from Dark Eras Companion which is a Pseudo-Gold.) So, having more Refinements than the typical ten as a concept is perfectly fine. Then come the two issues, however:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The number of Refinements you complete as a Promethean determine your Integrity stat as a mortal, 1-for-1. Since the Integrity stat caps out at 10, it's not possible to benefit from more than 10 Refinements beyond that Exceptional Success benefit you mentioned.</li> <li>That twelfth Refinement I mentioned, Pneuma, was a <i>failed</i> alternative to Aurum. Where Aurum revolved around understanding humans and humanity, Pneuma is the philosophy that salvation (i.e. the New Dawn) comes from God, and is granted to the Prometheans via Grace. Since the Great Work is supposed to be something that's ultimately done on <i>your own initiative</i> (though you can obviously have help from others), the effectiveness of the Pneuma Refinement was quite low, and as a result died out much like natural selection among sub-species. Presumably, the reason that there remains only 10 refinements (and Flux, but that doesn't really count since it ALSO doesn't progress the Pilgrimage) is because those are the ten among dozens of possible substitutes and alternatives that remain effective and viable for becoming human. Since becoming an Apostle ultimately requires becoming human, other Refinements which don't result in newborn humans don't generate Apostles. This is why there are no Apostles of Flux (to answer your last question) and no Apostles of Pneuma. They are spiritual/pseudo-genetic dead ends.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T04:18:57-08:00","id":1469083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1462867-refined-apostles-an-attempt-to-create-a-super-template?p=1467396#post1467396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for not answering your question right away, I haven't checked in here the past few days.<br /> <br /> So, the Mantle is an Athanor, and you can only make 1 Athanor per Refinement. Thus, if you created the Mantle, there's no chance of you creating a Refinement Furnace (I even made sure to state that you do NOT get a free Refinement Furnace from an exceptional success.) I don't know of any other way to refund the Vitriol besides that.<br /> <br /> Technically speaking, in the history of PtC there have been 12 refinements (the five simple, the five complex, Flux and then Pneuma from Dark Eras Companion which is a Pseudo-Gold.) So, having more Refinements than the typical ten as a concept is perfectly fine. Then come the two issues, however:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The number of Refinements you complete as a Promethean determine your Integrity stat as a mortal, 1-for-1. Since the Integrity stat caps out at 10, it's not possible to benefit from more than 10 Refinements beyond that Exceptional Success benefit you mentioned.</li> <li>That twelfth Refinement I mentioned, Pneuma, was a <i>failed</i> alternative to Aurum. Where Aurum revolved around understanding humans and humanity, Pneuma is the philosophy that salvation (i.e. the New Dawn) comes from God, and is granted to the Prometheans via Grace. Since the Great Work is supposed to be something that's ultimately done on <i>your own initiative</i> (though you can obviously have help from others), the effectiveness of the Pneuma Refinement was quite low, and as a result died out much like natural selection among sub-species. Presumably, the reason that there remains only 10 refinements (and Flux, but that doesn't really count since it ALSO doesn't progress the Pilgrimage) is because those are the ten among dozens of possible substitutes and alternatives that remain effective and viable for becoming human. Since becoming an Apostle ultimately requires becoming human, other Refinements which don't result in newborn humans don't generate Apostles. This is why there are no Apostles of Flux (to answer your last question) and no Apostles of Pneuma. They are spiritual/pseudo-genetic dead ends.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Please cite where there can only be one Athanor per Refinement. The idea of such a limit was quite a surprise to me. Also, you are right that integrity caps out at ten, but I was referring to a parallel chart that tracked other benefits such as the possibility of retaining one Alembic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T02:44:58-08:00","id":1469159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1462867-refined-apostles-an-attempt-to-create-a-super-template?p=1469083#post1469083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please cite where there can only be one Athanor per Refinement. The idea of such a limit was quite a surprise to me. Also, you are right that integrity caps out at ten, but I was referring to a parallel chart that tracked other benefits such as the possibility of retaining one Alembic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also thought that there could only be one Athanor per Refinement, but in fact after you ve raised the doubt i checked on the core book.<br /> The wording about it is not very clear, &quot;you put everything you learned into it&quot; could mean one try or one vitriol exp, i m not sure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}